Package: python3-chimera-spawn
Architecture: all
Section: python
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         python3-pydantic
Description: shared Python implementation for Chimera Spawn
 Shared models, errors, runtime helpers, and TLS/endpoint utilities used by
 both the Chimera Spawn client and server. This package does not install the
 CLI, server service, catalogs, or administrator group.

Package: chimera-spawn-client
Architecture: all
Depends: python3-chimera-spawn (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         python3-httpx,
         python3-rich,
         python3-ruamel.yaml,
         python3-typer,
         python3-websockets
Description: CLI for local and remote Chimera Spawn administration
 chimeractl administers a Chimera Spawn server over a local Unix socket or
 authenticated HTTPS/WSS. It does not install the privileged server, systemd
 service, catalogs, or systemd-nspawn runtime.

Package: chimera-spawn-server
Architecture: all
Depends: python3-chimera-spawn (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
         adduser,
         python3-aiohttp,
         python3-dbus-next,
         python3-jinja2,
         python3-ruamel.yaml,
         python3-watchfiles,
         systemd-container
Recommends: libnss-mymachines
Description: privileged Chimera Spawn server for systemd-nspawn hosts
 chimera-server is the durable lifecycle authority for managed systemd-nspawn
 containers. It serves a local Unix-domain API and, when explicitly
 configured, an authenticated TLS listener. Package installation does not
 enable remote network access or generate TLS keys.

Package: chimera-spawn
Architecture: all
Depends: chimera-spawn-client (= ${binary:Version}),
         chimera-spawn-server (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: systemd-nspawn container manager (complete installation)
 Metapackage that installs the Chimera Spawn client and server together for
 all-in-one hosts.
